[00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.280]   money on a good advisor agreement. The cash-starved startup running on the founder's savings doesn't
[00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:14.080]   want to, nor does the would-be advisor, who's well aware their most likely outcome is $0.
[00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.000]   Who wants to spend a few thousand in legal fees on that? So, you end up running on a stock option
